WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Anatomy of the Extraocular Muscles of the Bony Orbit.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Seven extraocular muscles reside in the orbit: levator palpebrae superioris, four rectus muscles, and two oblique muscles.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
The four recti (superior, inferior, medial, lateral) originate from the common annular tendon of Zinn surrounding the optic canal.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Innervation rule: LR6 SO4 R3. Lateral rectus by Abducens (CN VI), Superior oblique by Trochlear (CN IV), all others by Oculomotor (CN III).

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:00.000
The superior oblique tendon hooks through the fibrous trochlea at the superomedial orbital angle, acting to intort and depress the adducted eye.
